#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/rtc.rst:2
msgid "Real-time clock"
msgstr "Sat stvarnog vremena"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/rtc.rst:4
msgid ""
"The microcontroller's millisecond clock -- the one behind "
":func:`time.ticks_ms` and the timer subsystem -- counts elapsed time since "
"boot. The *real-time clock* (RTC) is separate hardware that tracks *wall-"
"clock* time -- year, month, day, hour, minute, second -- and keeps running "
"across resets and firmware updates. On cams with a backup battery wired to "
"the RTC supply, it survives full power loss as well."
msgstr ""
"Milisekundni sat mikrokontrolera -- onaj iza :func:`time.ticks_ms` i "
"podsustava mjerača vremena -- broji proteklo vrijeme od podizanja sustava. "
"*Sat stvarnog vremena* (RTC) zasebni je hardver koji prati *vrijeme zidnog "
"sata* -- godinu, mjesec, dan, sat, minutu, sekundu -- i nastavlja raditi "
"kroz resetiranja i ažuriranja ugrađenog programa (firmware). Na kamerama s "
"rezervnom baterijom spojenom na RTC napajanje, preživljava i potpuni gubitak"
" napajanja."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/rtc.rst:12
msgid "The RTC is what a deployed camera uses to:"
msgstr "RTC je ono što razmještena kamera koristi za:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/rtc.rst:14
msgid "Time-stamp log entries and saved images with a real date."
msgstr ""
"Vremensko označavanje zapisa dnevnika i spremljenih slika stvarnim datumom."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/rtc.rst:15
msgid "Pace long-running tasks that should not drift over weeks or months."
msgstr ""
"Tempiranje dugotrajnih zadataka koji ne bi smjeli odstupati tijekom tjedana "
"ili mjeseci."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/rtc.rst:19
msgid "The machine.RTC class"
msgstr "Klasa machine.RTC"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/rtc.rst:21
msgid ""
":class:`machine.RTC` is a singleton -- one RTC per camera, no id needed:"
msgstr ""
":class:`machine.RTC` je singleton -- jedan RTC po kameri, nije potreban id:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/rtc.rst:30
msgid ""
"The current date and time live in :meth:`~machine.RTC.datetime`. Calling it "
"with no arguments returns an 8-tuple:"
msgstr ""
"Trenutni datum i vrijeme nalaze se u :meth:`~machine.RTC.datetime`\\ . "
"Pozivanje bez argumenata vraća 8-torku:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/rtc.rst:39
msgid ""
"The fields are ``(year, month, day, weekday, hour, minute, second, "
"subseconds)``. To set the clock, pass an 8-tuple of the same shape back:"
msgstr ""
"Polja su ``(year, month, day, weekday, hour, minute, second, subseconds)``\\"
" . Za postavljanje sata proslijedite natrag 8-torku istog oblika:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/rtc.rst:47
msgid ""
"The camera keeps counting from that point. On a soft reset the time "
"continues uninterrupted; on a full power cycle the RTC falls back to its "
"default time unless a backup battery keeps it powered."
msgstr ""
"Kamera nastavlja brojati od te točke. Pri mekom resetiranju vrijeme se "
"nastavlja neprekinuto; pri potpunom ciklusu napajanja RTC se vraća na svoje "
"zadano vrijeme osim ako ga rezervna baterija drži napajanim."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/rtc.rst:53
msgid "When to set the RTC"
msgstr "Kada postaviti RTC"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/rtc.rst:55
msgid ""
"The RTC has no built-in way to know what time it is at boot. Three common "
"patterns set it:"
msgstr ""
"RTC nema ugrađen način da zna koliko je sati pri podizanju sustava. Tri "
"uobičajena obrasca ga postavljaju:"

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/rtc.rst:58
msgid ""
"**From a network time source.** Cams that come up on WiFi can fetch the time"
" with :mod:`ntptime` and write it to the RTC at startup."
msgstr ""
"**Iz mrežnog izvora vremena.** Kamere koje se podignu na WiFi mogu dohvatiti"
" vrijeme pomoću :mod:`ntptime` i upisati ga u RTC pri pokretanju."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/rtc.rst:61
msgid ""
"**From a host over USB.** A companion script on a laptop pushes the current "
"time when the cam is plugged in."
msgstr ""
"**Iz hosta preko USB-a.** Pomoćna skripta na prijenosnom računalu šalje "
"trenutno vrijeme kada se kamera priključi."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/rtc.rst:63
msgid ""
"**From a battery-backed external RTC chip.** A dedicated RTC IC (often on a "
"shield, with its own coin cell) keeps better long-term time than the on-chip"
" RTC and can be read at boot to seed :meth:`~machine.RTC.datetime`."
msgstr ""
"**Iz vanjskog RTC čipa s rezervnom baterijom.** Namjenski RTC IC (često na "
"shieldu, s vlastitom dugmastom baterijom) održava bolje dugoročno vrijeme od"
" RTC-a na čipu i može se očitati pri podizanju sustava kako bi se "
"inicijalizirao :meth:`~machine.RTC.datetime`\\ ."

#: ../../openmvcam/tutorial/hardware/production/rtc.rst:68
msgid ""
"Some applications never need to set the RTC at all. A duty-cycled \"wake "
"every 60 seconds and take a reading\" loop only cares about elapsed "
"intervals, which :func:`time.ticks_ms` and the timed-sleep patterns in "
":doc:`low-power` handle without ever consulting the RTC's wall-clock value."
msgstr ""
"Nekim aplikacijama uopće nikada nije potrebno postaviti RTC. Petlja s radnim"
" ciklusom \"probudi se svakih 60 sekundi i obavi očitanje\" brine samo o "
"proteklim intervalima, kojima :func:`time.ticks_ms` i obrasci tempiranog "
"spavanja u :doc:`low-power` rukuju a da nikada ne konzultiraju RTC-ovu "
"vrijednost zidnog sata."
